---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Case Study: PE-backed Healthcare Group — Stack10"
  description="How Stack10 deployed four interconnected AI systems across a 50-practice, $111M healthcare group — eliminating manual reporting and automating compliance."
  canonicalUrl="https://stack10.ai/case-studies/smile-partners/"
>

  <!-- ── CASE STUDY HERO ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="cs-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cs-hero-meta">
        <span class="badge badge-secondary">Case Study</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Healthcare</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Stack Build</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="cs-hero-title">
        PE-backed healthcare group. 50 practices. $111M revenue. One AI partner.
      </h1>
      <p class="cs-hero-sub">Four interconnected AI systems deployed across operations, compliance, finance, and reporting — eliminating manual work and giving leadership instant access to their own data.</p>

      <div class="cs-stats-bar" data-count-up>
        <div class="cs-stat">
          <span class="cs-stat-value" data-count-up-value>50</span>
          <span class="cs-stat-label">Practices connected</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-stat">
          <span class="cs-stat-value" data-count-up-value>300K+</span>
          <span class="cs-stat-label">Patient records queryable</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-stat">
          <span class="cs-stat-value" data-count-up-value>130</span>
          <span class="cs-stat-label">KPIs tracked in real time</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-stat">
          <span class="cs-stat-value" data-count-up-value>98%</span>
          <span class="cs-stat-label">Reduction in compliance processing</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── ENGAGEMENT OVERVIEW ──────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div class="cs-engagement-bar">
    <div class="container cs-engagement-inner">
      <span class="cs-engagement-label">How we engaged</span>
      <div class="cs-engagement-products">
        <div class="cs-engagement-product">
          <div class="cs-ep-badge">Stack Discover</div>
          <p class="cs-ep-desc">Mapped the data landscape across 50 practices — identifying where manual processes were costing the most time and where AI could have the highest impact before a single line of code was written.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-ep-connector" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-engagement-product">
          <div class="cs-ep-badge cs-ep-badge-primary">Stack Build</div>
          <p class="cs-ep-desc">Designed and deployed four interconnected production AI systems — intelligence layer, compliance agent, Xero reconciliation, and procurement workflow — each integrated with existing infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── BODY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div class="container cs-body">

    <!-- The Organisation -->
    <section class="cs-section" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="cs-section-title">The Organisation</h2>
      <p class="p1">A private equity-backed healthcare service organisation operating 50 practices across Australia and New Zealand — spanning WA, VIC, NSW, QLD, SA, NT and NZ.</p>
      <p class="p2">Under PE ownership, the business was under pressure to acquire multiple practices per quarter. Each acquisition added a new legal entity, a new Xero account, a new practice management system instance, and a new set of staff — all needing to report into head office.</p>
      <p class="p2">The result: a growing organisation with no unified view of itself.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="cs-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <!-- The Problem -->
    <section class="cs-section" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="cs-section-title">The Problem</h2>
      <p class="p1">The group had invested years building a data warehouse. Their finance team had spent significant effort getting data from Xero, their procurement platform, and their practice management software into one place.</p>
      <p class="p2">But having the data wasn't the problem. Getting answers from it was.</p>
      <div class="cs-callout">
        <p class="cs-callout-text">The entire analytics team was dedicated to extracting reports. Every question — how is Practice A tracking on conversion? What's procurement spend vs production at Practice B? — required multiple full-time resources to pull data, build a spreadsheet, and deliver a report.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="p2">At 50 practices, over 300,000 patient records, $111M in production and 130 KPIs to track — manual reporting was no longer viable.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="cs-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <!-- What Stack10 Built -->
    <section class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="cs-section-title">What Stack10 Built</h2>
      <p class="p1">Four interconnected solutions that fundamentally changed how the organisation operates.</p>

      <!-- Systems Overview Diagram -->
      <div class="cs-systems-map" data-reveal>
        <div class="cs-sys-card" data-reveal-child>
          <span class="cs-sys-num">01</span>
          <div class="cs-sys-info">
            <h4 class="cs-sys-name">Intelligence Layer</h4>
            <p class="cs-sys-desc">MCP agent on the data warehouse — plain-English queries for any leader</p>
          </div>
          <span class="cs-sys-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="cs-sys-connects">Leadership &amp; Regional Managers</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-sys-card" data-reveal-child>
          <span class="cs-sys-num">02</span>
          <div class="cs-sys-info">
            <h4 class="cs-sys-name">Compliance Agent</h4>
            <p class="cs-sys-desc">Autonomous WHS document retrieval and chemical register management</p>
          </div>
          <span class="cs-sys-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="cs-sys-connects">WHS Team</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-sys-card" data-reveal-child>
          <span class="cs-sys-num">03</span>
          <div class="cs-sys-info">
            <h4 class="cs-sys-name">Reconciliation Agent</h4>
            <p class="cs-sys-desc">AI-powered Xero classification across all entities with human sign-off</p>
          </div>
          <span class="cs-sys-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="cs-sys-connects">Finance Team</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-sys-card" data-reveal-child>
          <span class="cs-sys-num">04</span>
          <div class="cs-sys-info">
            <h4 class="cs-sys-name">Procurement Workflow</h4>
            <p class="cs-sys-desc">Automated spend reports pushed to Regional Managers with actions attached</p>
          </div>
          <span class="cs-sys-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="cs-sys-connects">Practice Managers</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- System 1 -->
      <div class="cs-system">
        <div class="cs-system-num">01</div>
        <div class="cs-system-body">
          <h3 class="cs-system-title">The Intelligence Layer</h3>
          <p class="cs-system-tag">MCP Agent · Plain-English Data Queries</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>The problem:</strong> Leadership couldn't get answers without waiting for someone to build a report.</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>What we built:</strong> An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that sits directly on top of their data warehouse. For each database view, we created tools with pre-configured SQL queries that allow an AI agent to query the database in real time. Any leader can now ask a question in plain English and get an answer in seconds.</p>
          <p class="cs-examples-label">Example use cases</p>
          <div class="cs-examples">
            <div class="cs-example">
              <p class="cs-example-label">Procurement vs production reporting</p>
              <p class="cs-example-desc">Previously required a dedicated analyst to compile across multiple systems. Now: ask the agent, get an instant report. Ask why spend is high at a specific practice and it digs deeper — surfacing the exact line items driving the variance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-example">
              <p class="cs-example-label">Doctor transition management</p>
              <p class="cs-example-desc">A practice was transitioning between treatment modalities. Finding every affected patient, reading their notes, and preparing a rebook list would traditionally take a week. The agent returned the full list in 2 minutes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-example">
              <p class="cs-example-label">Practice performance benchmarking</p>
              <p class="cs-example-desc">Ranking all 50 practices by production per active patient across a rolling 90-day window used to mean a half-day of analyst work pulling from multiple systems. Now it's one question — with drill-down into any practice that flags as an outlier.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-example">
              <p class="cs-example-label">New patient conversion tracking</p>
              <p class="cs-example-desc">Regional managers needed to know which practices were converting new patient consultations into treatment plans — and which weren't. Getting that answer used to take days of cross-referencing appointment and billing data. Now it's instant, by practice, by region, or across the group.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-example">
              <p class="cs-example-label">Month-end close readiness</p>
              <p class="cs-example-desc">With 50 separate Xero entities, checking which practices had unreconciled transactions before month-end close was a manual chase across the finance team. The agent now surfaces a complete close-readiness report across all entities in seconds.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-example">
              <p class="cs-example-label">Inventory discrepancy detection</p>
              <p class="cs-example-desc">Identifying which practices had the largest gap between ordered supplies and recorded usage — a key indicator of waste or theft — previously required pulling procurement and stock records manually for each location. Now surfaced in one query, with the ability to drill into individual SKUs per practice.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- System 2 -->
      <div class="cs-system">
        <div class="cs-system-num">02</div>
        <div class="cs-system-body">
          <h3 class="cs-system-title">The Compliance Agent</h3>
          <p class="cs-system-tag">WHS Automation · Autonomous Document Management</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>The problem:</strong> Every chemical agent in every practice needs a current Safety Data Sheet. Compiling the chemical register quarterly was manual, error-prone, and scaled linearly with every acquisition.</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>What we built:</strong> An autonomous AI compliance agent that integrates with procurement order history, identifies hazardous materials, and autonomously searches, validates, and centralises safety documentation from manufacturer websites. When it can't find a document with high certainty, it flags it rather than guessing — the WHS team shifted from data entry to exception management.</p>
          <div class="cs-before-after" data-reveal>
            <div class="cs-ba-before">
              <div class="cs-ba-header">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
                <span class="cs-ba-label">Before</span>
              </div>
              <div class="cs-ba-metric">80 hours</div>
              <ul class="cs-ba-list">
                <li>Manual compilation every quarter</li>
                <li>Scaled linearly with every acquisition</li>
                <li>Error-prone, always behind</li>
                <li>WHS team = full-time data entry</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-ba-divider" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-ba-after">
              <div class="cs-ba-header">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                <span class="cs-ba-label">After</span>
              </div>
              <div class="cs-ba-metric">&lt;1 hour</div>
              <ul class="cs-ba-list">
                <li>Autonomous document retrieval</li>
                <li>Scales instantly to new acquisitions</li>
                <li>94% success rate, always current</li>
                <li>WHS team = exception management only</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-metrics-inline" data-reveal>
            <div class="cs-metric-inline">
              <span class="cs-metric-inline-value">98%</span>
              <span class="cs-metric-inline-label">Reduction in processing time</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-metric-inline">
              <span class="cs-metric-inline-value">94%</span>
              <span class="cs-metric-inline-label">Autonomous success rate</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-metric-inline">
              <span class="cs-metric-inline-value">~$28K</span>
              <span class="cs-metric-inline-label">Estimated annual labour savings</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- System 3 -->
      <div class="cs-system">
        <div class="cs-system-num">03</div>
        <div class="cs-system-body">
          <h3 class="cs-system-title">The Reconciliation Agent</h3>
          <p class="cs-system-tag">Xero Integration · AI Financial Classification</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>The problem:</strong> Across 16+ separate Xero entities, high-value consumable spend was buried in a generic account code. Group leadership couldn't answer basic questions: How much are we spending per supplier per practice? Are practices over-ordering?</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>What we built:</strong> A full-stack reconciliation application that connects to every Xero entity, pulls invoice line items, uses AI classification to identify high-value consumable purchases, and writes reclassification journal entries back to Xero — with human sign-off at every step. For the first time, the group has visibility into their largest consumable cost category, automatically, across all entities.</p>
          <p class="cs-tech-note">FastAPI backend · Next.js + Shadcn/ui frontend · Multi-step AI pipeline (Haiku + Sonnet) · Supplier learning database · Full audit trail</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- System 4 -->
      <div class="cs-system">
        <div class="cs-system-num">04</div>
        <div class="cs-system-body">
          <h3 class="cs-system-title">Procurement Compliance Workflow</h3>
          <p class="cs-system-tag">Automated Reporting · Regional Manager Workflow</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>The problem:</strong> Practice managers needed to act on their numbers, but Regional Managers were buried managing multiple practices — too many numbers to stay on top of and communicate.</p>
          <p class="p2"><strong>What we built:</strong> An automated procurement reporting workflow. The system generates a report with relevant spend numbers and sends it to the Regional Manager. The RM reviews in their email, provides feedback via text, and approves. The report — with the RM's recommendations — is then sent directly to the practice manager with actionable items attached. Instead of practices having to pull their own reports, the data comes to them with specific actions. This workflow has become one of the primary tools driving procurement compliance across the group.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>

    <div class="cs-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <!-- Impact Numbers -->
    <section class="cs-section" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="cs-section-title">Impact across all four systems</h2>
      <p class="p2">Aggregated outcomes from the Intelligence Layer, Compliance Agent, Reconciliation Agent, and Procurement Workflow.</p>

      <div class="cs-impact-grid">

        <div class="cs-impact-category">
          <div class="cs-impact-category-header">
            <div class="cs-impact-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="cs-impact-category-title">Time Saved</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-impact-rows">
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">WHS compliance processing (annual)</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">316+ hrs</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Doctor transition workflows</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">1 week → 2 min</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Leadership report turnaround</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">Days → Seconds</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Month-end close readiness check</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">Hours → Instant</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Procurement report compilation (per cycle)</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">Eliminated</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-impact-category">
          <div class="cs-impact-category-header">
            <div class="cs-impact-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="23"/><path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="cs-impact-category-title">P&amp;L Impact</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-impact-rows">
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Direct WHS labour savings (annual)</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">~$28K</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Analytics team capacity redeployed</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">2–3 FTE</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Largest consumable cost visibility unlocked</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">Group-wide</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Supplier renegotiation leverage created</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">All 50 entities</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Procurement waste detection enabled</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">Per-SKU, per-practice</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-impact-category">
          <div class="cs-impact-category-header">
            <div class="cs-impact-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="cs-impact-category-title">Scale</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-impact-rows">
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Practices connected across all systems</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">50</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Patient records queryable in real time</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">300,000+</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">KPIs tracked automatically</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">130</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">Chemical SKUs under autonomous management</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">1,200+</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-impact-row">
              <span class="cs-impact-label">WHS autonomous document success rate</span>
              <span class="cs-impact-value">94%</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cs-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <!-- What's Next -->
    <section class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="cs-section-title">What&rsquo;s Next</h2>
      <p class="p2">Based on the success of these projects, Stack10 is now working with the group's in-house development team to:</p>
      <ul class="cs-next-list">
        <li>Replace the legacy PowerBI dashboard with a v2 platform built on the same intelligence layer</li>
        <li>Extend the MCP agent's capabilities deeper into practice-level operations — giving on-the-ground staff direct access to their own data</li>
        <li>Scale the reconciliation and compliance architecture to absorb new acquisitions automatically</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

  </div>

  <!-- ── CTA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="cs-cta">
    <div class="container cs-cta-inner">
      <h2 class="cs-cta-title">Ready to see what this looks like for your organisation?</h2>
      <p class="cs-cta-desc">Book a 30-minute Discovery Call. We'll tell you whether Stack10 is the right fit — and if not, we'll tell you honestly who is.</p>
      <div class="cs-cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          Book a Discovery Call
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17L17 7"/><path d="M7 7h10v10"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/case-studies/" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">View all case studies</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Page-scoped alpha tints (derived from design primitives) ── */
  :root {
    --cs-green-tag-bg:     color-mix(in oklch, var(--green-500) 10%, transparent);
    --cs-green-subtle-bg:  color-mix(in oklch, var(--green-500)  6%, transparent);
    --cs-green-subtle-border: color-mix(in oklch, var(--green-500) 25%, transparent);
    --cs-red-subtle-bg:    color-mix(in oklch, var(--destructive)  8%, transparent);
    --cs-red-subtle-border: color-mix(in oklch, var(--destructive) 22%, transparent);
  }

  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .cs-hero {
    background: var(--background);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: var(--space-16) 0 var(--space-12);
  }

  .cs-hero-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .cs-hero-title {
    font-size: var(--size-4xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-800);
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--foreground);
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .cs-hero-sub {
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    max-width: 56rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .cs-stats-bar {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-1);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-6);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .cs-stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    background: var(--card);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .cs-stat:last-child {
    border-right: none;
  }

  .cs-stat-value {
    font-size: var(--size-3xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-800);
    color: var(--primary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .cs-stat-label {
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* ── Engagement Bar ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  .cs-engagement-bar {
    background: var(--card);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .cs-engagement-inner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .cs-engagement-label {
    font-size: var(--size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    white-space: nowrap;
    padding-top: var(--space-1);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

